{"text": "BEAULIEU SANDHU LLP\nBarristers & Solicitors\n150 King Street West, Suite 2710\nToronto, ON  M5H 1J9\nT 416-555-0138   F 416-555-0139\n\nHarpreet K. Sandhu\nDirect: 416-555-0141\nhsandhu@beaulieusandhu.example\n\nMarch 2, 2026\n\nWITHOUT PREJUDICE\nDELIVERED BY COURIER AND EMAIL (gdeluca@lakeshorecustomhomes.example)\n\nLakeshore Custom Homes Inc.\nAttention: Mr. Giancarlo De Luca, President\n2380 Speers Road, Unit 14\nOakville, Ontario  L6L 5M2\n\nDear Mr. De Luca:\n\nRe:  Trillium Millwork & Cabinetry Ltd. -- unpaid invoices\n     48 Birchview Crescent, Oakville (the \"Cho residence\")\n     Our file no. 26-0193/HKS\n\nWe are the lawyers for Trillium Millwork & Cabinetry Ltd. (\"Trillium\").\n\nUnder a subcontract dated 2025-06-18, Trillium supplied and installed custom\nkitchen, pantry and library millwork at the home of Dr. Mei-Ling Cho, for which\nLakeshore is the general contractor. Trillium's last day on site was\nJanuary 23, 2026. Dr. Cho moved in the following week and, so far as we are aware,\nhas raised no deficiencies.\n\nThe following invoices remain unpaid:\n\n    Invoice     Date            Amount (incl. HST)\n    TM-4471     Nov. 28, 2025   $41,810.00\n    TM-4502     Dec. 19, 2025   $27,345.50\n    TM-4533     Jan. 30, 2026   $18,960.75\n                                Total     C$88,116.25\n\nTrillium's HST registration number, 84127 9036 RT0001, appears on each invoice. You have\nnot disputed any of them. On February 9 you told Trillium's controller, Wojciech Nowakowski,\nthat payment was \"waiting on the last draw.\" On February 20 your cheque no. 01187 for\n$25,000 was returned NSF. Mr. Nowakowski's messages since then have gone unanswered.\n\nDEMAND\n\nTrillium requires payment of C$88,116.25, plus interest at the contract rate of 18% per\nyear from each due date ($2,291.44 to today) and $45.00 in NSF charges, for a total of\n$90,452.69, by 5:00 p.m. on Thursday, March 12, 2026.\n\nPayment may be made by certified cheque payable to \"Beaulieu Sandhu LLP, in trust\", or by\nwire to our trust account:\n\n    Halton Community Credit Union\n    Transit / institution: 00412-828\n    Account: 1047882\n    Reference: 26-0193/HKS\n\nIf payment is not received by that time, our instructions are to preserve and perfect\nTrillium's lien against the Cho residence under section 31 of the Construction Act,\nR.S.O. 1990, c. C.30, and to start an action in the Superior Court of Justice against\nLakeshore and against you personally on the guarantee you signed on June 18, 2025. In\nthat case Trillium will also seek its costs and prejudgment interest under the Courts of\nJustice Act. Please note that a lien will name Dr. Cho as owner; we expect you would\nprefer to avoid that conversation with your client.\n\nThis letter is an offer to settle within the meaning of Rule 49. It is not a waiver of\nany of Trillium's rights, all of which are reserved.\n\nGovern yourself accordingly.\n\nYours very truly,\nBEAULIEU SANDHU LLP\n\nHarpreet K. Sandhu\nLSO No. 71842P\n\nc.  client (W. Nowakowski, wojciech@trilliummillwork.example)\n    É. Beaulieu", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "452 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Harpreet K. Sandhu", "Giancarlo De Luca", "Mei-Ling Cho", "Wojciech Nowakowski", "Dr. Cho", "W. Nowakowski"], "companies": ["BEAULIEU SANDHU LLP", "Lakeshore Custom Homes Inc.", "Trillium Millwork & Cabinetry Ltd.", "Trillium", "Lakeshore", "Beaulieu SANDHU LLP", "trilliummillwork"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Toronto", "Oakville", "Trillium Millwork & Cabinetry Ltd.", "Lakeshore Custom Homes Inc.", "Lakeshore", "Cho residence", "Superior Court of Justice"], "health": [], "sensitive": ["NSF"], "names": ["Harpreet K.", "Giancarlo", "Mei-Ling", "Wojciech", "BEAULIEU", "W. Nowakowski"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.10000000149011612, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "ur